    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Pioneer settlers in the 1850s—Irish, Scottish, and German—founded farms in Adams and Hazel Green Townships, attracted by fertile prairie soils for grain, livestock, and dairy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
